If that command fails because you don't have the required public key,
or that public key has expired, try the following commands to retrieve
or refresh it, and then rerun the 'gpg --verify' command.

  gpg --recv-keys 5DBE23D3905365267F8CC76AFDB952BD3F7356D6

As a last resort to find the key, you can try the official GNU
keyring:

  wget -q https://ftp.gnu.org/gnu/gnu-keyring.gpg
  gpg --keyring gnu-keyring.gpg --verify mes-0.28.tar.gz.sig

This release is based on the mes git repository, available as

  git clone https://git.savannah.gnu.org/git/mes.git

with commit c54282e9c7102e88374031d97ae7d448ce31603b tagged as v0.28.

For a summary of changes and contributors, see:

  https://git.sv.gnu.org/gitweb/?p=mes.git;a=shortlog;h=v0.28

or run this command from a git-cloned mes directory:

  git shortlog v0.27.2..v0.28

Alternatively, Mes can be installed using GNU Guix:

  guix pull
  guix install mes

NEWS

* Changes in 0.28 since 0.27.2
** Core
*** Evaluator is replaced by a compiler and a bytecode virtual machine.
*** Macro expander is written in Scheme.
*** Stack and Heap are now allocated separately.
*** Structs and Vectors are now Bytes with raw pointers to their elements.
*** Builtins are now indices to a static table.
*** initial-module is now a module instead of just an obarray.
*** Variables are now basic types and not records.
*** Builtins now fail throwing exceptions instead of halting the execution.
*** Overall, the interpreter performance has been improved by a 40% (execution
time).
** Mes
*** REPL accepts multiple return values.
*** Module eval-closure is removed.
*** current-environment is removed.
*** 4 new functions are added:
bytevector-fill!, procedure-name, procedure-arguments, procedure-disassemble
** MesCC
*** Memory used in global uninitialized arrays is vastly reduced.
** Noteworthy bug fixes
*** close-port now returns a value: *unspecified*.

See also <https://bootstrappable.org>.
Join bug-mes@gnu.org and #mes on irc.libera.chat for discussions.

